body:
@normanmaurer sorry, I made a mistake in my description. No `PrematureChannelClosureException` is raised. The problem is that https://github.com/netty/netty/blob/4.1/codec-http/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/codec/http/HttpObjectDecoder.java#L441 does not happen, because `HttpObjectDecoder` thinks that the channel was prematurely closed. I thinks this, because it's seeing `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` that was added by `HttpContentDecoder`, but that wasn't actually on the request.

My fix for this would be to effectively move https://github.com/netty/netty/blob/4.1/codec-http/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/codec/http/HttpObjectDecoder.java#L441 to somewhere around https://github.com/netty/netty/blob/4.1/codec-http/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/codec/http/HttpObjectDecoder.java#L606. That is, read and store whether the request was variable length just after reading the headers. Do you have a better idea?

Can you also please point me to a test for a similar kind of thing that I can use as a starting point.
